# paper.pdf — MISSING (institutional access required)

The primary Blattner et al. 1997 PDF (Science 277:1453-1462, doi:10.1126/science.277.5331.1453) is behind
the AAAS / Science.org paywall. Automated retrieval attempts made on 2026-07-05:

- https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.277.5331.1453  →  HTTP 403 (Cloudflare bot-check)
- https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/pmid/9278503/  →  HTTP 200 but Science 1997 is pre-PMC (HTML wrapper only, no PDF)
- https://europepmc.org/api/get?...  →  HTTP 404 (paper not in Europe PMC full-text)
- UNAM mirror (referenced in original attempt log)  →  unreachable

To fill this artifact, an institutional AAAS/Science subscription (ANL library, UChicago library) is
required. Fetch the PDF from the Science.org DOI landing page while authenticated, save as
`paper.pdf` (sibling of this file), then re-run `scripts/check_repl_dir_standard.py` to promote the
directory to "complete."

The replication itself does NOT depend on the primary PDF: all quantitative claims used in the
verdict are traceable from the PubMed abstract (PMID 9278503, verbatim in `extraction/marker.md`)
plus canonical EcoCyc/RegulonDB counts plus Murakami 2015 (PMC4696680) rRNA-operon crosscheck.
This file exists so that the missing-PDF condition is explicit and machine-checkable rather than
silently absent.
